":[],"red":[],"fl":[0,4,268400],"best":[[0,4,268400]],"xl":[],"bx":[],"nar":[{"lap":0,"text":"Varzi starts from pole; Nuvolari and Wimille complete the front row.","q":false,"c":0},{"lap":0,"text":"Chambost's Maserati refused to start and a mechanic was still working in vain with a handle when the Resident General dropped the flag at exactly 2 p.m. and the rest of the field went away.","q":true,"src":"goldenera.fi","c":5},{"lap":0,"text":"The acceleration of the Auto Union was superior and Varzi immediately took the lead followed by Etancelin and nineteen other competitors.","q":true,"src":"goldenera.fi","c":0},{"lap":1,"text":"Nuvolari soon passed Etancelin for second position.","q":true,"src":"goldenera.fi","c":10},{"lap":1,"text":"Varzi completes the first lap in 4m46s, Nuvolari about 100m behind, then Etancelin and Wimille.","q":false,"c":0},{"lap":2,"text":"Zanelli stops at the pits.","q":false,"c":12},{"lap":2,"text":"After the second lap Varzi led Nuvolari by 12 seconds followed by Wimille 31s behind and Etancelin.","q":true,"src":"goldenera.fi","c":0},{"lap":4,"text":"Varzi laps in 4m28.4s and pulls further away from Nuvolari.","q":false,"c":0},{"lap":4,"text":"Brunet arrives slowly at the pit and retires with a mechanical problem.","q":false,"c":20},{"lap":5,"text":"After five laps Varzi led Nuvolari by 43 seconds and Wimille by 56 seconds. Etancelin had gearbox trouble and had fallen back 1m27s.","q":true,"src":"goldenera.fi","c":0},{"lap":5,"text":"Falchetto abandons his old Maserati at El-Aou\u00efna with transmission problems.","q":false,"c":16},{"lap":5,"text":"Zehender went wide in the Sidi Fredj corner, spun, overturned the 6-cylinder Maserati and ended up in an orange orchard.","q":true,"src":"goldenera.fi","c":21},{"lap":6,"text":"On the sixth lap Etancelin attacked Nuvolari, who was now struggling with an engine problem, and passed him for second position.","q":true,"src":"goldenera.fi","c":2},{"lap":7,"text":"Nuvolari pits to change plugs; Balestrero retires his Maserati.","q":false,"c":10},{"lap":8,"text":"Soffietti (broken supercharger) and Ghersi (gearbox) have stopped at the pits.","q":false},{"lap":8,"text":"After eight laps Varzi was leading Wimille by 1m10s and Etancelin by 2m30s and the Auto Union driver was able to slow down a bit to save his car.","q":true,"src":"goldenera.fi","c":0},{"lap":9,"text":"Nuvolari is back in the pits; Zanelli and Siena retire.","q":false,"c":10},{"lap":12,"text":"Nuvolari retires his Alfa with lubrication trouble after a lengthy stop.","q":false,"c":10},{"lap":12,"text":"After one hour Wimille is 1m14s behind Varzi; Etancelin third.","q":false,"c":1},{"lap":14,"text":"Sommer passes Comotti for fifth and then Farina for fourth.","q":false,"c":8},{"lap":15,"text":"At around lap 15 Wimille had a scary moment when the bonnet of his Bugatti came off and almost hit his head.","q":true,"src":"goldenera.fi","c":1},{"lap":16,"text":"Etancelin is down to top gear only, losing 20 seconds a lap.","q":false,"c":2},{"lap":17,"text":"After 17 laps Wimille had lost 1m46.4s to Varzi while Etancelin was 4m39s behind and falling back.","q":true,"src":"goldenera.fi","c":1},{"lap":21,"text":"While the mechanics worked on the car, chain smoker Varzi jumped out and quietly smoked a cigarette.","q":true,"src":"goldenera.fi","c":0},{"lap":21,"text":"After the 1m27s stop Varzi rejoined the race, 11 seconds in front of Wimille, who relentlessly was chasing the faster Auto Union.","q":true,"src":"goldenera.fi","c":0},{"lap":22,"text":"Etancelin makes his fuel stop; Sommer moves up to third. F\u00e9vrier stops to replace a broken wheel.","q":false,"c":2},{"lap":25,"text":"On the 25th lap Rey missed the corner at Soucra, destroyed his left rear wheel and spun.","q":true,"src":"goldenera.fi","c":9},{"lap":26,"text":"Sommer retires with a broken connecting rod.","q":false,"c":8},{"lap":27,"text":"Varzi leads Wimille by 2m30s; Mablot retires with a broken steering rod.","q":false,"c":0},{"lap":40,"text":"Varzi takes the chequered flag; Wimille second, 3m49.6s behind; Etancelin third, two laps down, then Comotti, Farina, Chambost, Hartmann and \"Raph\".","q":false,"c":0}]}